+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

This port disables Lynx features that launch external programs, including
shell, editor, mail, and clipboard helpers. Local file access is limited by
an unveil(2) policy; arbitrary paths outside the current directory and the
listed state files may be unavailable.

Run Lynx as an unprivileged user with HOME set to an existing directory.
Startup fails closed if HOME cannot be resolved. Set LYNX_TEMP_SPACE and
LYNX_SAVE_SPACE to directories outside HOME and its ancestors. An existing
HOME/Downloads symlink is left inaccessible by the sandbox. The configured
temp/save directories and /tmp remain writable areas; keep that in mind for
sensitive local data. Do not use this sandboxed package as root.

The sandbox is single-process and does not provide site isolation or a
separate renderer. The pledge/unveil rules constrain Lynx itself only.
